cpuidle: Free the names of PM domains when removing them

The PSCI and RISC-V SBI drivers both remove PM domains on a failed or
deferred probe, and both forget the name dt_idle_pd_alloc() allocated.

The PSCI patch is tested: kmemleak listed the 11 names on a Moto G Power
(2021), and lists none with it. The RISC-V SBI patch is the same change and
is compile tested only, with no RISC-V hardware to hand. They are separate
so each can go through its own maintainer.
